## Included in this repository

### electrs

`docs/electrs-0.11.1-knots-29.4.2-rpc.patch` is a patch against electrs
(<https://github.com/romanz/electrs>, MIT licence, Copyright (C) 2018, Roman Zeyde) for a Knots
29.4.2 RPC. The header and proof-of-work code in this tree was written for this project and
checked against that lineage.

### libsecp256k1

Channel signatures are verified through the `xbt402` reference's `coincurve` backend, which builds
libsecp256k1 (<https://github.com/bitcoin-core/secp256k1>, MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2013 Pieter
Wuille).

### Bitcoin Knots test vectors

`tests/vectors/` holds header vectors captured from a Bitcoin Knots BLAKE2b regtest node and used
to test the header code. They are recorded chain data.

## Python libraries

The tests install the packages in `requirements.txt` (mcp, anyio, cryptography) and import the
`xbt402` reference. They are not vendored. Their licence texts must accompany any distribution
that includes them.
